# /services/acpid — the ACPI service: it runs the firmware's AML.
#
# svcmgr launches acpid post-handover on every boot, as a provider.
# `provides` makes svcmgr create acpid's service endpoint, serve its RECV as
# bootstrap cap[0], and publish two SENDs on it:
#   * acpid.power:auth — POWER_AUTHORITY-tokened (1 << 63), for the sleep,
#     reset and power-button (WAIT_EVENT) requests; seed-only, and pwrmgr is
#     the only recipe seeding it.
#   * acpid.deny:deny  — a no-authority twin (sentinel token 1) that the
#     SLEEP/RESET/WAIT_EVENT gate rejects; svctest uses it to assert the deny
#     path.
# `seed = devmgr.acpi` delivers cap[1], a SEND on devmgr's registry badged
# REGISTRY_QUERY_AUTHORITY | ACPI_AUTHORITY, through which acpid acquires the
# tables, the FADT's register blocks and the SCI, each operation region
# devmgr grants it and each configuration-space access, and pushes each PCI
# host bridge's _OSC grant, windows and interrupt routes
# (services/acpid/README.md). acpid is the only recipe seeding it.
# `logd.flush` delivers cap[2], the LOG_FLUSH_AUTHORITY-badged SEND on the
# master log endpoint, whose only authority is logd's flush barrier: acpid
# waits on it, bounded, between its line naming a reset or sleep register
# write and the write, which ends the machine and the lines logd holds
# unwritten with it (services/logd/docs/ipc-interface.md § Flush barrier).
#
# `restart = on_failure`: svcmgr re-creates acpid and re-serves a fresh RECV
# on the persistent endpoint, so pwrmgr's acpid.power SEND survives a
# crash-restart; acpid re-acquires its capabilities from devmgr and runs its
# start-up again; devmgr keeps the results of the first start (and the
# memory regions it granted).
# `critical = no`: devmgr never waits on acpid, so the system runs on
# without it, without the _OSC grant and the routes it pushes, and on x86-64
# without pwrmgr's shutdown and reboot, whose requests then fail after
# pwrmgr's 30 s bound on each acpid call, and without the power button.
binary    = /services/acpid
priority  = 16
restart   = on_failure
critical  = no
namespace = none
provides  = acpid.power:auth acpid.deny:deny
seed      = devmgr.acpi logd.flush
